 "rules": "Special election for the remainder of Marco Rubio's term (ends January 3, 2029). Plurality winner; no runoff. Three candidates on the ballot: Ashley Moody (R), Angie Nixon (D), Neil Gillespie (no party affiliation). In-person early voting ran October 24-31 in all 67 counties (some counties offered extra days). Under Florida law, vote-by-mail ballots must be received by 7 p.m. local time on Election Day (overseas voters have up to 10 days for federal races) and may be canvassed before Election Day; Florida results are usually reported on election night. Polls close at 7 p.m. local time (the western Panhandle is on Central time). Sources: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_special_election_in_Florida ; https://www.wusf.org/politics-issues/2026-10-26/florida-voters-almost-2-8m-surge-past-22-midterm-benchmark-as-early-voting-goes-statewide",
